{
  "_comment": "🪝️ Specification vectors for the `hook` verb. Each vector is one native invocation — the event slug the caller named, the client, the tool it reports and the payload it piped — and states the bytes the verb writes and the code it exits with. The environment and the test-file resolver are inert, so a vector is a pure function of its request.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "a-neutral-agent-event-in-json-mode-writes-one-record",
      "request": { "event": "agent.started", "client": "claude-code", "second": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "json": true, "input": {} }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-neutral-agent-event-in-plain-mode-writes-nothing",
      "request": { "event": "agent.started", "client": "claude-code", "second": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "json": false, "input": {} }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-blocked-terminal-command-refuses-with-exit-code-two",
